---
name: jvm-package-import
description: a JVM package is importable, and the names in it are ordinary calls
---

# A JVM package is importable

`scalascript.typeddata` is a Scala library, not an `.ssc` module — v3 used to refuse this import
with four candidate FILE paths, a message about a file that cannot exist. The package is declared
in `v3/jvm-classpath.sh`; the names resolve one at a time through the plugin SPI, so the kernel
asks no class loader anything and invariant I-1 is untouched.

A FENCE IS REQUIRED HERE and that is the language's rule, not this test's: a bare `.ssc` is code
throughout and its import lines are never scanned.

```scalascript
import scalascript.typeddata.{DatasetWirePartition}

// Construction goes through the companion's `apply`, with each argument fitted to its DECLARED
// parameter type — v3 has one integer and Scala has `Int` and `Long`, and only the signature says
// which was meant.
val p = DatasetWirePartition(7, Vector())

// A field is read by NAME: `Product` is the only thing that knows the names, so they are recorded
// as the value crosses.
println(p.partitionId)
println(p.values.length)
```
